== Pickle ==

Place @red onion{1}(peeled and finely sliced) and @cucumber{1}(thinly sliced) in a bowl and pour over @rice vinegar{3%tbsp}, @sugar{2%tsp}, and @white sesame seeds{1%tsp}. Scrunch everything to coat and leave to pickle, mixing occasionally while you prepare the curry.


== Curry ==

Heat #saucepan{} over medium heat with @vegetable oil{1%tbsp}. Add @onion{1}(diced) and @carrot{1}(diced) with a pinch of @sea salt{1%tsp} and cook down until soft and starting to caramelise. Stir through @garlic{4%cloves}(minced) and @ginger{2cm}(minced) for ~{2%minutes}, then add @turmeric{1%tsp} and @curry powder{2%tbsp} and @plain flour{1%tbsp}. Stir in @tomato paste{1%tbsp}, @soy sauce{1%tbsp}, and @brown sugar{1%tbsp}. Pour in @coconut milk{400ml} and @vegetable stock{350ml} and bring to a low simmer. Use a hand blender to blend until smooth. Taste to season.


== Fried Tofu ==

Drain @tofu{500g} and slice into 1cm thick rectangles. Place @plain flour{4%tbsp}, @sea salt{1%tsp}, and @plant-based milk{150ml} in a bowl and whisk to a smooth batter. Place @panko breadcrumbs{50g}, @desiccated coconut{25g}, and @black sesame seeds{1%tbsp} in a shallow bowl. Dip the tofu slices in the batter to coat, shaking off any excess, then dip in the crumb mix until coated on all sides. Transfer to a tray while you repeat with the remaining tofu. Add enough @vegetable oil{about 0.5cm} to coat the base of a pan and bring to a high heat, testing if a few breadcrumbs sizzle. Lay the tofu slices into the pan until crispy and golden, then flip over and fry the other side. Transfer to a tray lined with kitchen paper and repeat with the remaining slices, careful not to overcrowd the pan.


== Serve ==

Divide the curry between bowls alongside cooked rice. Top with slices of the fried tofu and pickled vegetables. Top with fresh @cilantro{5g}(leaves) and serve with wed